Don't nest functions

function scoreAndReturn()
{
    score();
    return;  // implicit return is ok
}

Avoid long variable names

You don't have to use verbose variable names. While being more readable, the trade-off is that they have to typed out more often. The variable $json is a good example how the length of a variable name doesn't affect code quality even though the variable contains critical information. It should be shortened to $result or $response.

function scoreAndReturn()
{
    $json = score();

    return $json;  // implicit return is ok
}

Make proper use of the return value

